<article class="env-lemma" id="060V">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/060V">Lemma <span data-tag="060V">74.6.2</span>.</a> Let $X$ be an algebraic space over a scheme $S$. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. Let $\{ f_ i : X_ i \to X\} _{i \in I}$ be an fpqc covering such that each $f_ i^*\mathcal{F}$ is an $\mathcal{O}_{X_ i}$-module of finite presentation. Then $\mathcal{F}$ is an $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module of finite presentation. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from the case of schemes, see Descent, Lemma <a href="/tag/05B0" data-tag="05B0">35.7.3</a>, by étale localization. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>